,{"id":"chris","nameParsed":{"literal":"Chris Calloway","given":"Chris","family":"Calloway"},"name":"Chris Calloway","email":"cbc@unc.edu","affiliations":["University of North Carolina"]},{"id":"rowan","nameParsed":{"literal":"Rowan Cockett","given":"Rowan","family":"Cockett"},"name":"Rowan Cockett","email":"rowan@curvenote.com","affiliations":["Curvenote"]},{"id":"sanhita","nameParsed":{"literal":"Sanhita Joshi","given":"Sanhita","family":"Joshi"},"name":"Sanhita Joshi","email":"sanhita.joshi@gmail.com","affiliations":["Deloitte"]},{"id":"charles","nameParsed":{"literal":"Charles Lindsey","given":"Charles","family":"Lindsey"},"name":"Charles Lindsey","email":"lindseycster@gmail.com","affiliations":["Aptos"]},{"id":"hongsup","nameParsed":{"literal":"Hongsup Shin","given":"Hongsup","family":"Shin"},"name":"Hongsup Shin","email":"hongsup.shin@pm.me","affiliations":["Arm"]}],"venue":{"title":"Python in Science Conference","short_title":"SciPy","url":"https://scipy2024.scipy.org","doi":"10.25080/issn.2575-9752","number":"23rd","location":"Tacoma, Washington","date":"July 8 - July 14, 2024","series":"Proceedings of the Python in Science Conference","issn":"2575-9752","publisher":"SciPy"},"keywords":["prefect","workflow orchestration","dask","zarr","fisheries acoustics"],"affiliations":[{"id":"eScience Institute, University of Washington","name":"eScience Institute, University of Washington"},{"id":"Scientific Software Engineering Center, University of Washington","name":"Scientific Software Engineering Center, University of Washington"},{"id":"Applied Physics Laboratory, University of Washington","name":"Applied Physics Laboratory, University of Washington"},{"id":"GDI","name":"GDI"},{"id":"SLB","name":"SLB"},{"id":"University of North Carolina","name":"University of North Carolina"},{"id":"Curvenote","name":"Curvenote"},{"id":"Deloitte","name":"Deloitte"},{"id":"Aptos","name":"Aptos"},{"id":"Arm","name":"Arm"}],"id":"scipy-2024-valentina_staneva","bannerOptimized":"https://pub.curvenote.com/0192f9e5-e76d-70ec-b175-9c5b57c04e4a/public/banner-8e6aef2c394247d4ed2d4ea0d1f8839d.webp","thumbnailOptimized":"https://pub.curvenote.com/0192f9e5-e76d-70ec-b175-9c5b57c04e4a/public/thumbnail-ea89402ee92e4f39e51cbd66f35b61b7.webp","bibliography":[],"index":"main","pages":[]}],"id":"0192f9e5-e76d-70ec-b175-9c5b57c04e4a"},"page":{"kind":"Article","sha256":"7ecdcc967d3aaff40ef132a0665b7d4ad4319e04c9cb162dd99cb9633e25e306","slug":"main","location":"/main.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Echodataflow: Recipe-based Fisheries Acoustics Workflow Orchestration","parts":{"abstract":{"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","data":{"part":"abstract"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"With the influx of large data from multiple instruments and experiments, scientists are wrangling complex data pipelines that are context-dependent and non-reproducible. We demonstrate how we leverage Prefect ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"hEAvy1QwED"},{"type":"citeGroup","kind":"parenthetical","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"cite","identifier":"prefect","label":"prefect","kind":"parenthetical","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":211},"end":{"line":1,"column":219}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefect, 2024","key":"mWB00IzBKR"}],"enumerator":"1","key":"qVql5an6EK"}],"key":"Ov5tj9SNO0"},{"type":"text","value":", a modern orchestration framework, to facilitate fisheries acoustics data processing. We built a Python package Echodataflow ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"GXys4dGHZX"},{"type":"citeGroup","kind":"parenthetical","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"cite","identifier":"echodataflow","label":"echodataflow","kind":"parenthetical","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":347},"end":{"line":1,"column":360}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Echodataflow, 2024","key":"tB7eMJlLkI"}],"enumerator":"2","key":"cUe87hZUrO"}],"key":"GSbkgKnmrC"},{"type":"text","value":" which 1) allows users to specify workflows and their parameters through editing text “recipes” which provide transparency and reproducibility of the pipelines; 2) supports scaling of the workflows while abstracting the computational infrastructure; 3) provides monitoring and logging of the workflow progress. Under the hood, Echodataflow uses Prefect to execute the workflows while providing a domain-friendly interface to facilitate diverse fisheries acoustics use cases. We demonstrate the features through a typical ship survey data processing pipeline.","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"Nj99oAfsAS"}],"key":"BAm3wsDiMw"}],"key":"ND8vfvCVkJ"}],"key":"dN4Jfctiyb"},"frontmatter":{"title":"Echodataflow: Recipe-based Fisheries Acoustics Workflow Orchestration","authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Valentina Staneva","given":"Valentina","family":"Staneva"},"name":"Valentina Staneva","corresponding":true,"email":"vms16@uw.edu","roles":["Funding acquisition","Project administration","Resources","Software","Supervision","Writing – original draft"],"affiliations":["eScience Institute, University of Washington"],"id":"contributors-myst-generated-uid-0"},{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Soham Butala","given":"Soham","family":"Butala"},"name":"Soham Butala","email":"sbutala@uw.edu","roles":["Software","Writing – review \u0026 editing"],"affiliations":["eScience Institute, University of Washington"],"id":"contributors-myst-generated-uid-1"},{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Landung (Don) Setiawan","given":"Landung (Don)","family":"Setiawan"},"name":"Landung (Don) Setiawan","email":"landungs@uw.edu","roles":["Conceptualization","Software"],"affiliations":["Scientific Software Engineering Center, University of Washington"],