ence","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Figure ","key":"WLFxYQvXfy"},{"type":"text","value":"3","key":"KV0nimAL8C"}],"identifier":"fig:echodataflow_overview","label":"fig:echodataflow_overview","kind":"figure","template":"Figure %s","enumerator":"3","resolved":true,"html_id":"fig-echodataflow-overview","key":"NBG7DZY6FK"},{"type":"text","value":" we provide an overview of ","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"Ncl3ltF2rL"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"echodataflow","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"IX3wqWs8Cf"},{"type":"text","value":"’s framework. At the center we see several steps of an echosounder data processing pipeline: ","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"LSMV1g8a3s"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"open_raw","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"ypiIgr2wZ6"},{"type":"text","value":", ","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"VvKibpRXy8"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"combine_echodata","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"Su8h3fUANV"},{"type":"text","value":", ","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"xkGv2HRbuH"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"compute_Sv","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"C8iFiKtClR"},{"type":"text","value":", ","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"NCDCPSL5KT"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"compute_MVBS","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"smtEZa2UF3"},{"type":"text","value":", ","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"TWgHPrPk6s"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"frequency_differencing","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"IkLwK0erIf"},{"type":"text","value":", which produce echo classificaton results using a simple threshold-based criterion. All these functions exist in the ","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"NCHa4zkpQV"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"echopype","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"uPTtccJGYF"},{"type":"text","value":" package, and are wrapped by ","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"xXHtm5Mqz1"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"echodataflow","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"xqecw6ZfTp"},{"type":"text","value":" into pre-defined stages. Prefect executes the stages on a Dask cluster which can be started locally or can be externally set up. These ","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"rsBpn2nxc2"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"echopype","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"j7wCEAaIK2"},{"type":"text","value":" functions already support distributed operations with Dask, and thus the integration with Prefect within ","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"C1mh2nKpC4"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"echodataflow","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"oOr8pDerxr"},{"type":"text","value":" is natural. Dask clusters can be set up on a variety of platforms: local computers, cloud virtual machines, kubernetes ","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"zJSJjwOZM1"},{"type":"citeGroup","kind":"parenthetical","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"cite","identifier":"kubernetes","label":"kubernetes","kind":"parenthetical","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1258},"end":{"line":66,"column":