Code","value":"datastore.yaml","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"key":"X0wTYZ33pC"},{"type":"text","value":" with a data storage configuration for a ship survey. In this scenario the goal is to process data from the Joint U.S.-Canada Integrated Ecosystem and Pacific Hake Acoustic Trawl Survey ","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"key":"tShqk2Ve7d"},{"type":"citeGroup","kind":"parenthetical","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"cite","identifier":"nwfsc_fram_2022","label":"NWFSC_FRAM_2022","kind":"parenthetical","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":234},"end":{"line":91,"column":250}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Northwest Fisheries Science Center, Fishery Resource Analysis and Monitoring Division, 2022","key":"iU3fRTF1nL"}],"enumerator":"4","key":"nFPb8O0kHW"}],"key":"VhQjm1brn6"},{"type":"text","value":" which are publicly available on an ","key":"khTfwf57cm"},{"type":"abbreviation","title":"Amazon Web Services","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AWS","key":"NJFqdFbuwa"}],"key":"RSpuc8urTI"},{"type":"text","value":" S3 bucket hosted by ","key":"bMpKc43gx1"},{"type":"abbreviation","title":"National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"NOAA","key":"QPlaeUKNHI"}],"key":"wAXdxLLiUF"},{"type":"text","value":" National Centers for Environmental Information Acoustics (NCEA) Archive ","key":"u6nAoUuYWu"},{"type":"citeGroup","kind":"parenthetical","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"cite","identifier":"wall_2016","label":"wall_2016","kind":"parenthetical","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":389},"end":{"line":91,"column":399}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wall, 2016","key":"Gm8kNgxedo"}],"enumerator":"20","key":"nUVSoa9LfJ"}],"key":"olCLAU0FOt"},{"type":"text","value":". The archive contains data from many surveys dating back to 1991 (~280TB). The configuration allows to pass parameters specifying the ship, survey, and sonar model names and select the subset of files belonging only to the survey of interest. The output destination is set to a private S3 bucket belonging to the user (within an ","key":"saRJvwhy61"},{"type":"abbreviation","title":"Amazon Web Services","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AWS","key":"wMveBo2WII"}],"key":"alLixqKtJ4"},{"type":"text","value":" account different from the input one), and the credentials are passed through a ","key":"jM7X7G6ok6"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"block_name","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"key":"iw0w05jN5v"},{"type":"text","value":". The survey contains ~4000 files, and one can set the group option to combine the files into survey-specific groups: based on the transect information provided in the ","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"key":"kSot2LgMeS"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"transect_group.txt","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"key":"BtPKvp4HiG"},{"type":"text","value":" file. One can further use regular expressions to subselect other subgroups based on needs.","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"key":"JkWLZdGaGq"}],"key":"M6jqJFsTzC"},{"type":"comment","value":" :::{figure} datastore_config.png\n:label: fig:datastore_config\n**Data Storage Configuration:** The input is data from a ship survey data on and S3 data on the NCEA archive. The output goes to an S3 bucket on another AWS account. Credentials are stored in blocks.\n:::\n","key":"laF9LJpvGK"},{"type":"comment","value":":name: datastore-config\nData Storage Configuration\n","key":"V6JzgMV6em"},{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","value":"# datastore.yaml\n\nname: Bell_M._Shimada-SH1707-EK60\nsonar_model: EK60\nraw_regex: (.*)-?D(?P\u003cdate\u003e\\w{1,8})-T(?P\u003ctime\u003e\\w{1,6})\nargs:\n  urlpath: s3://ncei-wcsd-archive/data/raw/{{ ship_name }}/{{ survey_name }}/{{ sonar_model }}/*.raw\n  parameters:\n    ship_name: Bell_M._Shimada\n    survey_name: SH1707\n    sonar_model: EK60\n  storage_options:\n    anon: true\n  group:\n    file: ./transect_group.txt\n    storage_options:\n      block_name: echodataflow-aws-credentials\n      type: AWS\n  group_name: default_group\n  json_export: true\n  raw_json_path: s3://echodataflow-workground/combined_files/raw_json\noutput:\n  urlpath: \u003cYOUR-S3-BUCKET\u003e\n  overwrite: true\n  retention: false\n  storage_options:\n    block_name: echodataflow-aws-credentials\n    type: AWS","position":{"start":{"line":103,"column":1},"end":{"line":132,"column":1}},"key":"H1jvLKsm1A"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":134,"column":1},"end":{"line":134,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pipeline Configuration","position":{"start":{"line":134,"column":1},"end":{"line":134,"column":1}},"key":"iVD1FnZxCS"}],"identifier":"pipeline-configuration","label":"Pipeline Configuration","html_id":"pipeline-configuration","implicit":true,"enumerator":"4.2","key":"tu4WeDBuIs"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The pipeline configuration file’s purpose is to list the stages of the processing pipeline and the computational set-up for their execution. Below we show an example ","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"ae44bvVSKB"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pipeline.yaml","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"ZdrqYEjA9K"},{"type":"text","value":" file which cofigures a pipeline with several stages: ","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"jY8SOcM7FT"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"open_raw","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"hagsmCPsFl"},{"type":"text","value":", ","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"TAuufpiGmY"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"combine_echodata","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"IckJXqmNVm"},{"type":"text","value":", ","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"TUVVdRwNav"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"compute_Sv","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"WzNEXKojHL"},{"type":"text","value":", ","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"eZVsu32OGd"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"compute_MVBS","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"x9kN6W1eyg"},{"type":"text","value":". Each stage is executed as a separate Prefect subflow (a component of a Prefect workflow), and one can specify additional options on whether to store the raw files. ","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"tRHUYq2oNp"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"echodataflow","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"poLmSCLiKN"},{"type":"text","value":" requires access to a Dask cluster: it can be either created on the fly by setting the ","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"uxspwTuARJ"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"use_local_dask","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"cBipE4OSjv"},{"type":"text","value":" to ","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"zwpZRTezN1"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"XpZUcy9Bab"},{"type":"text","value":", or an IP address of an already running cluster can be provided. Individual stages may require different cluster configurations to efficiently execute the tasks. Those can be specified with the additional ","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"as8XrnLIli"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prefect_config","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"MEFgNWKDRB"},{"type":"text","value":" option through which the user can set a specific Dask task runner or the number of retries. Managing retries is essential for handling transient failures, such as connectivity issues, ensuring the stages can be re-executed without any manual interference if a failure occurs.","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"vA5kmj1RV0"}],"key":"VdzdDi9G1A"},{"type":"comment","value":"\n:::{figure} pipeline_config.png\n:label: fig:pipeline_config\n**Pipeline Configuration:** The pipeline consists of two stages: `echodataflow_open_raw` and `echodataflow_compute_TS` and will run on a local cluster.\n:::\n","key":"KMysE7IErX"},{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","value":"# pipeline.yaml\n\nactive_recipe: standard\nuse_local_dask: true\nn_workers: 4\nscheduler_address: tcp://127.0.0.1:61918\npipeline:\n  - recipe_name: standard\n    stages:\n      - name: echodataflow_open_raw\n        module: echodataflow.stages.subflows.open_raw\n        options:\n          save_raw_file: true\n          use_raw_offline: true\n          use_offline: true\n        prefect_config:\n          retries: 3\n      - name: echodataflow_combine_echodata\n        module: echodataflow.stages.subflows.combine_echodata\n        options:\n          use_offline: true\n      - name: echodataflow_compute_Sv\n        module: echodataflow.stages.subflows.compute_Sv\n        options:\n          use_offline: true\n      - name: echodataflow_compute_MVBS\n        module: echodataflow.stages.subflows.compute_MVBS\n        options:\n          use_offline: true\n        external_params:\n          range_meter_bin: 20\n          ping_time_bin: 20S","position":{"start":{"line":145,"column":1},"end":{"line":178,"column":1}},"key":"TiEcq8lSgZ"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":180,"column":1},"end":{"line":180,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Logging Configuration","position":{"start":{"line":180,"column":1},"end":{"line":180,"column":1}},"key":"tjQDKspGSG"}],"identifier":"logging-configuration","label":"Logging Configuration","html_id":"logging-configuration","implicit":true,"enumerator":"4.3","key":"xy5ic4POfw"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":182,"column":1},"end":{"line":182,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, the outcomes of each stage are logged. The logs can be stored in ","position":{"start":{"line":182,"column":1},"end":{"line":182,"column":1}},"key":"KfP9MzW90T"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".json","position":{"start":{"line":182,"column":1},"end":{"line":182,"column":1}},"key":"fi9kLsf0ax"},{"type":"text","value":" or plain text files, and the format of the entries can be specified in the configuration file as displayed below. The ","position":{"start":{"line":182,"column":1},"end":{"line":182,"column":1}},"key":"Z09rnp80wt"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"json","position":{"start":{"line":182,"column":1},"end":{"line":182,"column":1}},"key":"XTl5YlTqXa"},{"type":"text","value":" format allows searching through the logs for a specific key.","position":{"start":{"line":182,"column":1},"end":{"line":182,"column":1}},"key":"QLqjbercQR"}],"key":"a2eUnNtnJ9"},{"type":"comment","value":" :::{figure} logging_config.png\n:label: fig:logging_config\n**Logging Configuration:** The logs are written to a local `echodataflow.log` file in a plain text form based on the format specification\n:::\n","key":"eNePc05g5v"},{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","value":"# logging.yaml\n\nversion: 1\ndisable_existing_loggers: False\nformatters:\n  json:\n    format: '[%(asctime)s] %(process)d %(levelname)s %(mod_name)s:%(func_name)s:%(lineno)s - %(message)s'\n  plaintext:\n    format: '[%(asctime)s] %(process)d %(levelname)s %(mod_name)s:%(func_name)s:%(lineno)s - %(message)s'\nhandlers:\n  logfile:\n    class: logging.handlers.RotatingFileHandler\n    formatter: plaintext\n    level: DEBUG\n    filename: echodataflow.log\n    maxBytes: 1000000\n    backupCount: 3\n\nloggers:\n  echodataflow:\n    level: DEBUG\n    propagate: False\n    handlers: [logfile]","position":{"start":{"line":190,"column":1},"end":{"line":214,"column":1}},"key":"DCiD6E0mkp"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":216,"column":1},"end":{"line":216,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"In this case the logs are stored in the plain text file ","position":{"start":{"line":216,"column":1},"end":{"line":216,"column":1}},"key":"tyrs5ZKVFR"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"echodataflow.log","position":{"start":{"line":216,"column":1},"end":{"line":216,"column":1}},"key":"qnw3oC2xH7"},{"type":"text","value":". Below we show an example of output logs.","position":{"start":{"line":216,"column":1},"end":{"line":216,"column":1}},"key":"eZen3n8zLR"}],"key":"WgtvD85MF4"},{"type":"comment","value":":::{figure} log_output.png\n:label: fig:log_output\n**Log Output:** An example of an output log of file processing failure. The leading indicators for each entry are: date, process id, log level, followed by the module, function, line number, followed by the message.\n:::\n","key":"ccMBUHeBa3"},{"type":"code","lang":"log","value":"[2024-06-06 17:32:08,945] 51493 ERROR apply_mask.py:EK60_SH1707_Shimada2_applymask.zarr:147 - Computing apply_mask\n[2024-06-06 17:32:08,946] 51493 ERROR file_utils.py:file_utils:147 - Encountered Some Error in EK60_SH1707_Shimada0\n[2024-06-06 17:32:08,946] 51493 ERROR file_utils.py:file_utils:147 - 'source_ds' must have coordinates 'ping_time' and 'range_sample'!\n[2024-06-06 17:32:08,946] 51493 ERROR file_utils.py:file_utils:147 - Encountered Some Error in EK60_SH1707_Shimada1\n[2024-06-06 17:32:08,946] 51493 ERROR file_utils.py:file_utils:147 - 'source_ds' must have coordinates 'ping_time' and 'range_sample'!\n[2024-06-06 17:32:08,946] 51493 ERROR file_utils.py:file_utils:147 - Encountered Some Error in EK60_SH1707_Shimada2\n[2024-06-06 17:32:08,946] 51493 ERROR file_utils.py:file_utils:147 - 'source_ds' must have coordinates 'ping_time' and 'range_sample'!","position":{"start":{"line":224,"column":1},"end":{"line":232,"column":1}},"key":"FzdO4jNjwT"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":234,"column":1},"end":{"line":234,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"In ","position":{"start":{"line":234,"column":1},"end":{"line":234,"column":1}},"key":"P09ZuuOa75"},{"type":"crossReference","identifier":"workflow-logging","label":"workflow-logging","kind":"heading","position":{"start":{"line":234,"column":4},"end":{"line":234,"column":21}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Section ","key":"p5eROrtjY4"},{"type":"text","value":"7","key":"u8KrKzuGLx"}],"template":"Section %s","enumerator":"7","resolved":true,"html_id":"workflow-logging","key":"lxiARs4jmz"},{"type":"text","value":", we provide more information on logging options.","position":{"start":{"line":234,"column":1},"end":{"line":234,"column":1}},"key":"tNnmZ7YCKv"}],"key":"IzoVj7JnCJ"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":236,"column":1},"end":{"line":236,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Workflow Execution","position":{"start":{"line":236,"column":1},"end":{"line":236,"column":1}},"key":"To2iiDg0Bg"}],"identifier":"workflow-execution","label":"Workflow Execution","html_id":"workflow-execution","implicit":true,"enumerator":"5","key":"SYqP2NmBiR"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":238,"column":1},"end":{"line":238,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"To convert a scientific pipeline into an executable Prefect workflow, one needs to organize its components into flows, sublfows, and tasks (the key objects of Prefect’s execution logic). Usually, the stages of a pipeline are organized into flows and subflows, while the individual pieces of work within the stage are organized into tasks. In practice, flows, subflows, and tasks are all Python functions, and they differ in how we want to execute them (e.g. concurrently/sequentially, w/o retries), and what we want to track during execution (e.g. input/outputs, state logging, etc.). In ","position":{"start":{"line":238,"column":1},"end":{"line":238,"column":1}},"key":"SvdHiYAb0c"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"echodataflow","position":{"start":{"line":238,"column":1},"end":{"line":238,"column":1}},"key":"beYhIDIiUL"},{"type":"text","value":" we organize the typical echosounder processing stages into subflows (flows within the main workflow), while the operations on different files (or groups of them) are individual tasks. We describe how functions are organized in the ","position":{"start":{"line":238,"column":1},"end":{"line":238,"column":1}},"key":"mlHOjMf8ja"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"open_raw","position":{"start":{"line":238,"column":1},"end":{"line":238,"column":1}},"key":"ebgp1GOuUW"},{"type":"text","value":" stage, which reads the files from raw format, parses the data, and writes them into a ","position":{"start":{"line":238,"column":1},"end":{"line":238,"column":1}},"key":"ebvlAXxzVs"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"zarr","position":{"start":{"line":238,"column":1},"end":{"line":238,"column":1}},"key":"qcYzWyM24x"},{"type":"text","value":" format. The ","position":{"start":{"line":238,"column":1},"end":{"line":238,"column":1}},"key":"jBd03pj2vx"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"echodataflow_open_raw","position":{"start":{"line":238,"column":1},"end":{"line":238,"column":1}},"key":"H3nhSP9k2H"},{"type":"text","value":" function is decorated as a flow, and is one of many subflows of the full workflow. This function processes all files.","position":{"start":{"line":238,"column":1},"end":{"line":238,"column":1}},"key":"klvUc0QHjQ"}],"key":"umZeSvM8m5"},{"type":"comment","value":"\n:::{figure} flow_task.png\n:label: fig:flow_task\n**Decorating Functions into Flows \\\u0026 Tasks:** The flow `echdataflow_open_raw` calls the task `process_raw` (processing a single file) within a loop to process all files\n:::\n","key":"Vp9bsQqwfb"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","value":"@flow\n@echodataflow(processing_stage=\"Open-Raw\", type=\"FLOW\")\ndef echodataflow_open_raw(\n    groups: Dict[str, Group], config: Dataset, stage: Stage, prev_stage: Optional[Stage]\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Process raw sonar data files and convert them to zarr format.\n\n    Args:\n        config (Dataset): Configuration for the dataset being processed.\n        stage (Stage): Configuration for the current processing stage.\n        prev_stage (Stage): Configuration for the previous processing stage.\n\n    Returns:\n        List[Output]: List of processed outputs organized based on transects.","position":{"start":{"line":247,"column":1},"end":{"line":263,"column":1}},"key":"K4ve51HzxW"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":265,"column":1},"end":{"line":265,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"echodataflow_open_raw","position":{"start":{"line":265,"column":1},"end":{"line":265,"column":1}},"key":"Wg1ijmYPOb"},{"type":"text","value":" contains a loop which iterates through all file groups and applies the ","position":{"start":{"line":265,"column":1},"end":{"line":265,"column":1}},"key":"FkhzqHxcxT"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"process_raw","position":{"start":{"line":265,"column":1},"end":{"line":265,"column":1}},"key":"Mfba6BBPoq"},{"type":"text","value":" function which operates on a single group and is decorated as a task. All tasks will be executed on the Dask cluster.","position":{"start":{"line":265,"column":1},"end":{"line":265,"column":1}},"key":"klWctMaScB"}],"key":"XAHLg5x30q"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","value":"for name, gr in groups.items():\n        for raw in gr.data:\n            new_processed_raw = process_raw.with_options(\n                task_run_name=raw.file_path, name=raw.file_path, retries=3\n            )\n            future = new_processed_raw.submit(raw, gr, working_dir, config, stage)\n            futures[name].append(future)\n","position":{"start":{"line":267,"column":1},"end":{"line":276,"column":1}},"key":"ZxtWkxGhLD"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","value":"@task()\n@echodataflow()\ndef process_raw(\n    raw: EchodataflowObject, group: Group, working_dir: str, config: Dataset, stage: Stage\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Process a single group of raw sonar data files.","position":{"start":{"line":278,"column":1},"end":{"line":286,"column":1}},"key":"l46BUIl8Qw"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":288,"column":1},"end":{"line":288,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Workflow Monitoring","position":{"start":{"line":288,"column":1},"end":{"line":288,"column":1}},"key":"jCLPNEqkLV"}],"identifier":"workflow-monitoring","label":"Workflow Monitoring","html_id":"workflow-monitoring","implicit":true,"enumerator":"6","key":"KZpcyXk2TS"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":290,"column":1},"end":{"line":290,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"One of the main advantages of using orchestration frameworks is that they usually provide tools to monitor the workflow execution. The integration with Prefect allows leveraging Prefect’s dashboard (Prefect UI) for monitoring the execution of the flows. The dashboard can be run locally and within Prefect’s online managed system (Prefect Cloud). The local version provides an entirely open source framework for running and monitoring workflows. ","position":{"start":{"line":290,"column":1},"end":{"line":290,"column":1}},"key":"tR16prHrZO"},{"type":"crossReference","position":{"start":{"line":290,"column":1},"end":{"line":290,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Figure ","key":"NOr4OYjWnM"},{"type":"text","value":"4","key":"YHI1KfrSh4"}],"identifier":"fig:flow_sequence_expanded","label":"fig:flow_sequence_expanded","kind":"figure","template":"Figure %s","enumerator":"4","resolved":true,"html_id":"fig-flow-sequence-expanded","key":"YczgvXmjJ3"},{"type":"text","value":" shows the view of completed runs within the dashboard. The progress can be monitored while the flows are in progress.","position":{"start":{"line":290,"column":1},"end":{"line":290,"column":1}},"key":"RZBEkdCEzD"}],"key":"Y46d0MEQNJ"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"https://pub.curvenote.com/0192f9e5-e76d-70ec-b175-9c5b57c04e4a/public/flow_sequence_expand-80f43d86ad2ee31c17f2ecf9c283e759.png","alt":"Flow Runs: Log of completed runs in Prefect UI. The stages (subflows) are executed sequentially. One can expand the view of an individual flow and see the tasks computed (asynchronously) within it.","data":{"altTextIsAutoGenerated":true},"key":"HnYut0UEzH","urlSource":"flow_sequence_expanded.png","urlOptimized":"https://pub.curvenote.com/0192f9e5-e76d-70ec-b175-9c5b57c04e4a/public/flow_sequence_expand-80f43d86ad2ee31c17f2ecf9c283e759.webp"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":294,"column":1},"end":{"line":294,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"captionNumber","kind":"figure","label":"fig:flow_sequence_expanded","identifier":"fig:flow_sequence_expanded","html_id":"fig-flow-sequence-expanded","enumerator":"4","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Figure ","key":"nA7JHf41Nk"},{"type":"text","value":"4","key":"kiUnpsvBz4"},{"type":"text","value":":","key":"KCzvezN5jn"}],"template":"Figure %s:","key":"ZE2SYASLDQ"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":294,"column":1},"end":{"line":294,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Flow Runs:","position":{"start":{"line":294,"column":1},"end":{"line":294,"column":1}},"key":"gqCaFlkJOT"}],"key":"aRmLrUDpaH"},{"type":"text","value":" Log of completed runs in Prefect UI. The stages (subflows) are executed sequentially. One can expand the view of an individual flow and see the tasks computed (asyn